[[File:Akagi-jinja (Miyosawa) torii.JPG|thumb|250px|right|{{center|Grand Torii}}]]
'''Akagi Shrine''' (赤城神社) is a {{ill|shrine|ja|神社|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/shrine|qq=}} located in Miyosawa-cho, {{ill|Maebashi City|ja|前橋市|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Maebashi City|qq=}}, {{ill|Gunma Prefecture|ja|群馬県|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gunma Prefecture|qq=}}.
It is a {{ill|Shikinaisha|ja|式内社|1=Shikinaisha|2=ja|3=式内社|qq=draft|1=Shikinaisha|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikinaisha|qq=}} ({{ill|Meishin Taisha|ja|名神大社|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Meishin Taisha|qq=}}) {{ill|Ronsha|ja|論社|1=candidate shrines|2=ja|3=論社|lt=candidate|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ronsha|13=User:Immanuelle/candidate shrines|qq=}}, as well as a Nomiya Ronsha of {{ill|Ueno Province|ja|上野国|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ueno Province|qq=}}, and formerly a {{ill|Prefectural Shrine|ja|県社|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Prefectural Shrine|qq=}}.

Although its official name is "Akagi Shrine", to distinguish it from other Akagi Shrines it is also called "'''Miyosawa Akagi Shrine''' (みよさわあかぎじんじゃ)". It is one of the principal shrines, presumed to be the main shrine among approximately 300 Akagi Shrines across the country, mainly in the {{ill|Kanto region|ja|関東地方|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kanto region|qq=}}.

== Overview ==
Located on the southern hillside of {{ill|Mount Akagi|ja|赤城山|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mount Akagi|qq=}} in central {{ill|Gunma Prefecture|ja|群馬県|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gunma Prefecture|qq=}}, the shrine was once regarded as having two shrines (East and West) before the Meiji era, but later became a single shrine. The approach splits into three directions: one with the first torii leading south toward the {{ill|Grand Torii|ja|大鳥居|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Grand Torii|qq=}} and the Ōogomachi area, one east toward Naegashima, and one west toward Ichinoseki. The road continuing in the Ōogomachi direction still retains a pine avenue planted during the Edo period.

Both the main hall and the middle gate are designated as important cultural properties by the prefecture. Along the approach, about 500 meters south of the main hall, stands the Soumon (main gate), also designated as an important cultural property. Additionally, between the worship hall and the middle gate, immediately in front of the middle gate, is the "Tawara Cedar", a natural monument designated by Gunma Prefecture. The shrine grounds also include a "Jindai Moji Stele" erected in March 1870 (Meiji 3), regarded as an artifact of the restoration of ancient Shinto, and designated as an important cultural property by the city.

== Worshipped Deities (Saijin) ==
{{see also|{{ill|Saijin|ja|祭神|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Saijin|qq=}}}}
* {{ill|Akagi God|ja|赤城神|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Akagi God|qq=}} (Akagi no Kami)
* {{ill|Toyoki Irihiko-no-mikoto|ja|豊城入彦命|1=Toyokiirihiko-no-Mikoto|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Toyoki Irihiko-no-mikoto|13=User:Immanuelle/Toyokiirihiko-no-Mikoto|qq=}} (Toyoki Irihiko-no-mikoto)
* {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大己貴命|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|qq=}} (Ōkuninushi-no-mikoto)

== History ==
[[File:MountAkagi.jpg|thumb|250px|right|{{center|{{ill|Mount Akagi|ja|赤城山|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mount Akagi|qq=}} (Sacred Object)}}]]
=== Establishment ===
The establishment date is unknown. According to the shrine’s tradition, in ancient times when {{ill|Toyoki Irihiko-no-mikoto|ja|豊城入彦命|1=Toyokiirihiko-no-Mikoto|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Toyoki Irihiko-no-mikoto|13=User:Immanuelle/Toyokiirihiko-no-Mikoto|qq=}} came to rule {{ill|Kozuke Province|ja|上毛野国|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kozuke Province|qq=}}, he enshrined {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大己貴命|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|qq=}}.

About 1.3 km uphill from the shrine, a ritual site centered on a stone called the "Hitsuishi" remains, suggesting ancient worship practices.

=== Chronological Overview ===
