== History ==
[[File:MountAkagi.jpg|thumb|250px|right|{{center|{{ill|Mount Akagi|en|Mount Akagi|qid=Q415251|lt=Mount Akagi|1=Mount Akagi}} (Sacred Object)}}]]
=== Establishment ===
The establishment date is unknown. According to the shrine’s tradition, in ancient times when {{ill|Toyoki Irihiko-no-mikoto|ja|豊城入彦命|1=Prince Toyokiirihiko|2=ja|3=豊城入彦命|qid=Q11633375|1=Prince Toyokiirihiko|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Toyoki Irihiko-no-mikoto|13=User:Immanuelle/Prince Toyokiirihiko|qq=}} came to rule {{ill|Kozuke Province|ja|上毛野国|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kozuke Province|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 上毛野国造|1=Kamitsuke no Kuni no Miyatsuko|comment=changed title based on wikidata|qid=Q11359471}}, he enshrined {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大己貴命|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 大国主}}.

About 1.3 km uphill from the shrine, a ritual site centered on a stone called the "Hitsuishi" remains, suggesting ancient worship practices.

